meta {
  name: me
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{vipa}}/api/v1/auth/me
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Returns the current user, or 401 with an ApiError body when no session is attached.

  It was the only endpoint locked down by US-005; since US-009 the business endpoints
  answer 401 the same way. Run it before login to see the 401, and again after logout to
  check the session really died server-side rather than just losing its cookie.

  The role in the body is what the rest of the collection is read against: a 403 further
  on means the role shown here is not in that endpoint's list, not that the request is
  malformed.
}
